# MCL - Multiple interactive commands

## Enable command sequences

MCL is off by default. In [CONFIG](CONFIG.HLP), choose F, then B to enable
its 128-byte persistent allocation. Save and cold boot. This reduces maximum
COM capacity by 128 bytes; [STAT MEM](STAT.HLP) reports the resulting limit.

## Separate commands

```text
VER;DIR
VAR X=NEW;VAR X
```

Semicolons separate interactive commands outside double quotes. Quotes must
balance across the whole line before the first command runs. Empty segments
are skipped. The input limit stays 127 characters and history records the
original line once. [VAR](VAR.HLP) expansion occurs separately for each selected
command, so later commands observe earlier assignments.

## Returns and cancellation

Ordinary program returns and warm boots continue the pending remainder.
Recognized CCP/BDOS errors or cancellation discard it. A program that prints
its own error and returns normally still continues the sequence.

STARTUP and [SUBMIT](SUBMIT.HLP) records retain literal semicolons. XSUB and
program input do not consume pending commands. MCL does not add FLOW features.
